  "text": "8. | Which the following is/are not true with respect to the decision of the Supreme\namong\nCourt of India in Vellore Citizens Welfare Forum v. Union of India (AIR 1996 SC 2715)?\n1. This was a PIL against the pollution caused by discharge of untreated effluent from\ntanneries and other industries.\nIl. The Court refused to recognise that a balance must be struck between the economy\nand the environment.\nlil. The Court accepted the traditional concept that development and ecology are\nopposed to each other.\niV. The Court reviewed the development of the concept of sustainable development in\nthe international sphere.\nThe Supreme Court held that the precautionary principle and the polluter pays\nprinciple are part of International environmental law and not of municipal law.\nA.  Onlyi, iiiandv\nOnlvil\nB. ii\nonly iti\nC. lil, ivandv\nD. Onlyivandv",
